    // Determine display names for expanded commands
    // Logic for display name:
    // If command_name provided:
    // - For non-param case: if command_name.len()==1 and total>1? We saw first gets custom, rest default? Implementation earlier observed: 2 commands, 1 name "name1": first Benchmark name1, second default (sleep 0.02). So mapping: if command_name.len()==1 and base_commands.len()>1, first gets custom, others get default (expanded). But what about 3 commands, 1 name "a": we saw first got "a", rest default. Yes.
    // - If command_name.len() == base_commands.len() (non-param): each gets corresponding custom.
