        // JSON command: What does JSON "command" field contain?
        // Earlier we observed:
        // - For "echo hello" with param x=a, no placeholder: JSON command = "echo hello" (original, not expanded)
        // - For "echo hello {x}" with param x=a: JSON command = "echo hello a" (expanded)
        // - For custom name "Base" with param x=a, with placeholder: JSON command = "Base" (custom name)
        // - For custom name "Base" with param x=a, without placeholder: JSON command = "Base" (custom name)
        // So JSON command is: if custom name provided, use custom base name (without suffix) ??? For N custom case, JSON also uses custom name.
